        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Avril Lavigne, Scott Spock, Lauren Christy, Graham Edwards, Celine Dion\n- Works: \"Sk8er Boi\", Let Go\n- Groups: The Matrix\n- Topics: music releases, songwriting, record sales\n\nFacts:\n- In 2002, \"Sk8er Boi\" was released as the second single from Avril Lavigne's debut album Let Go.\n- Avril Lavigne is a Canadian singer-songwriter, and \"Sk8er Boi\" means \"skater boy.\"\n- Avril Lavigne and The Matrix wrote \"Sk8er Boi.\"\n- The Matrix consisted of Scott Spock, Lauren Christy, and Graham Edwards.\n- The Matrix produced \"Sk8er Boi.\"\n- Since her professional debut, Avril Lavigne has sold more than 40 million albums and over 50 million singles worldwide.\n- Since her professional debut, Avril Lavigne has been the second-best-selling Canadian female artist of all time behind Celine Dion.",
